  "details": "The following notification is displayed as \"1 hour ago\" in the VRChat client (Build `1938`), but \"2 hours ago\" on VRChat Home website, when viewed 1 hour 48 minutes after receiving the notification (at 08:48):\n\n```\n\n2026.11.12 07:00:43 Debug      -  Received Notification: <Notification from username:***, sender user id:usr_*** to usr_6fa4abc5-9952-4a0a-97de-b3598fbf6a5c of type: boop, id: not_d1fe0375-26de-4ec0-af08-4bd9a0ccf3c0, created at: 11/12/2026 07:00:40 UTC, details: {{emojiId=default_heart, emojiVersion=, inventoryItemId=}}, type:boop, m seen:False, message: \"*** Booped You!\">\n\n```\n\nExpected result: The time shown should be either floored or rounded to the nearest hour in both places. I'm not sure which one is more appropriate.\n\nActual result: \"hours ago\" is floored in client (1 hour), but rounded to the nearest hour (2 hours) on the VRChat Home website.\n\nDuplicate bug report in the client category: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/vrchat-home-and-the-vrchat-client-display-hours-ago-in-notifications-inconsisten",
